Investigate a signal with competing physical explanations (@cm-monitoring-cause: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../../../engineering/mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/sources/Systems-Engineering-Handbook-NASA.lingua#r_7ZQFZ9E1NAVG27SE2R5S24PDBQ", #source "../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Statistical-Handbook.lingua#r_6S3221KSX1KKGPJNXKC3N022NN", #clean-manufacturing "Connect-a-monitoring-signal-to-a-proportionate-response.lingua#r_14SFA69Q0ZBZ89SWK9K08X0QR0") { r_1DBCZNKZTTP4TG3YP0A1CS17A8
**Read:** [Systems Engineering Handbook — NASA](../../../engineering/mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/sources/Systems-Engineering-Handbook-NASA.lingua#r_7ZQFZ9E1NAVG27SE2R5S24PDBQ), analysis of verification results; [Measurement Process Characterization — NIST/SEMATECH](../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Statistical-Handbook.lingua#r_6S3221KSX1KKGPJNXKC3N022NN), process modelling and experimental design. Revisit the three surface investigations.

A chart detects incompatibility with a reference model; it does not establish why. A particle-rate increase could reflect a changed source, changed transport, a changed measurement response or altered sampling. An apparent correlation with a maintenance event is evidence to investigate, not an automatic causal identification.

Map candidate causes through the source–transport–observation chain. Predict what each explanation would change in other quantities and choose an observation that distinguishes them. Include shared causes: a utility disturbance might affect both production and the instrument used to inspect it.

A before/after comparison can be confounded by product mix, season, operator, sampling or calibration. Where appropriate, a comparison state, repeated intervention or randomized benign model study can separate effects. Preserve observations that disagree with the preferred explanation.

**Work:** Create three explanations for one simulated signal and specify a different predicted observation for each. Use the existing physical balances to test plausibility. Explain which conclusion is supported, which remains tentative and what evidence would change the account.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
